# Cedar Hollow M4 — baseline Suricata ruleset for the router's
# zone-enterprise-facing interface. Complements, not replaces, the
# Zeek + sensor/detect.py baseline-allowlist layer that does the real
# work in this repo — see docs/architecture.md's detection design.
#
# Suricata's own protocol-anomaly rules for Modbus ship with the
# package (/etc/suricata/rules/modbus-events.rules) — they catch
# malformed/invalid Modbus PDUs, unsolicited responses, and request
# floods, things a byte-level parser is better placed to catch than a
# log-correlation script. `.rules` files have no include directive, so
# router/Dockerfile concatenates that file with this one at build time
# rather than duplicating its contents here.

# S03/S05-adjacent: any Modbus write function (05/06/0F/10) arriving on
# zone-enterprise's interface toward the relay port. This interface
# only ever carries traffic between an attacker container and the
# router in the M4 topology — normal HMI/historian traffic lives
# entirely on zone-ops and never crosses here — so *any* Modbus write
# seen on this wire is inherently the thing the scenario library is
# built to teach, not a false-positive-prone heuristic.
alert modbus any any -> any 502 (msg:"OT-RANGE Modbus write on zone-enterprise boundary"; modbus: function 5; classtype:attempted-admin; sid:9000001; rev:1;)
alert modbus any any -> any 502 (msg:"OT-RANGE Modbus write on zone-enterprise boundary"; modbus: function 6; classtype:attempted-admin; sid:9000002; rev:1;)
alert modbus any any -> any 502 (msg:"OT-RANGE Modbus write on zone-enterprise boundary"; modbus: function 15; classtype:attempted-admin; sid:9000003; rev:1;)
alert modbus any any -> any 502 (msg:"OT-RANGE Modbus write on zone-enterprise boundary"; modbus: function 16; classtype:attempted-admin; sid:9000004; rev:1;)

# S01-adjacent: any Modbus traffic at all on this boundary is recon by
# definition (no legitimate service originates from zone-enterprise) —
# a lower-severity catch-all so the analyst sees the reconnaissance
# too, not just the moment it turns into a write.
alert modbus any any -> any 502 (msg:"OT-RANGE Modbus traffic from zone-enterprise"; classtype:network-scan; sid:9000005; rev:1;)
